    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nWhen trying to open mini.files in a file that doesn't exist, it throws an error and doesn't open.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.0-dev+785-g44afd0744\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open any file\r\n2. `:!rm %`\r\n3. Try to open mini.files\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nIt should open the parent directory of the file that was deleted, for example if you deleted `~/.config/foo` and it should just open `~/.config`\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nIt throws an error and doesn't open",
